H6562.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 6561;
Meaning: to discontinue
KJV renders: break off.

H6563.strongs:
Origin: from 6561;
Meaning: rapine; also a fork (in roads)
KJV renders: crossway, robbery.

H6564.strongs:
Origin: from 6561;
Meaning: soup (as full of crumbed meat)
KJV renders: broth. See also 4832.

H6565.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to break up (usually figuratively), i.e. to violate, frustrate
KJV renders: × any ways, break (asunder), cast off, cause to cease, × clean, defeat, disannul, disappoint, dissolve, divide, make of none effect, fail, frustrate, bring (come) to nought, × utterly, make void.

H6566.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to break apart, disperse, etc.
KJV renders: break, chop in pieces, lay open, scatter, spread (abroad, forth, selves, out), stretch (forth, out).

H6567.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to separate, literally (to disperse) or figuratively (to specify); also (by implication) to wound
KJV renders: scatter, declare, distinctly, shew, sting.

H6568.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 6567;
Meaning: to specify
KJV renders: distinctly.

H6569.strongs:
Origin: from 6567;
Meaning: excrement (as eliminated)
KJV renders: dung.

H6570.strongs:
Origin: the same as 6569;
Meaning: Peresh, an Israelite
KJV renders: Peresh.

H6572.strongs:
Origin: or פַּתְשֶׁגֶן; of foreign origin;
Meaning: a transcript
KJV renders: copy.

H6574.strongs:
Origin: perhaps by compounding 6567 and 6504 (in the sense of straddling) (compare 6576);
Meaning: the crotch (or anus)
KJV renders: dirt.

H6575.strongs:
Origin: from 6567;
Meaning: exposition
KJV renders: declaration, sum.

H6576.strongs:
Origin: a root apparently formed by compounding 6567 and that of 6518 (compare 6574);
Meaning: to expand
KJV renders: spread.

H6577.strongs:
Origin: of Persian origin;
Meaning: Parshandatha, a son of Haman
KJV renders: Parshandatha.

H6578.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to break forth; rushing;
Meaning: Perath (i.e. Euphrates), a river of the East
KJV renders: Euphrates.

H6579.strongs:
Origin: of Persian origin;
Meaning: a grandee
KJV renders: (most) noble, prince.

H6580.strongs:
Origin: probably from an unused root meaning to disintegrate;
Meaning: stupidity (as a result of grossness or of degeneracy)
KJV renders: extremity.

H6581.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to spread
KJV renders: spread.

H6582.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to tear in pieces
KJV renders: pull in pieces.

H6583.strongs:
Origin: probably from 6582; liberation;
Meaning: Pashchur, the name of four Israelites
KJV renders: Pashur.

H6584.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to spread out (i.e. deploy in hostile array); by analogy, to strip (i.e. unclothe, plunder, flay, etc.)
KJV renders: fall upon, flay, invade, make an invasion, pull off, put off, make a road, run upon, rush, set, spoil, spread selves (abroad), strip (off, self).

H6585.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to stride (from spreading the legs), i.e. rush upon
KJV renders: go.

H6586.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root (identical with through the idea of expansion);
Meaning: to break away (from just authority), i.e. trespass, apostatize, quarrel
KJV renders: offend, rebel, revolt, transgress(-ion, -or).

H6587.strongs:
Origin: from 6585;
Meaning: a stride
KJV renders: step.

H6588.strongs:
Origin: from 6586;
Meaning: a revolt (national, moral or religious)
KJV renders: rebellion, sin, transgression, trespass.

H6589.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to dispart (the feet or lips), i.e. become licentious
KJV renders: open (wide).

H6590.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) corresponding to 6622;
Meaning: to interpret
KJV renders: make (interpretations), interpreting.

H6591.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from 6590;
Meaning: an interpretation
KJV renders: interpretation.

H6593.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 6580 as in the sense of comminuting;
Meaning: linen (i.e. the thread, as carded)
KJV renders: flax, linen.

H6594.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 6593;
Meaning: flax; by implication, a wick
KJV renders: flax, tow.

H6595.strongs:
Origin: from 6626;
Meaning: a bit
KJV renders: meat, morsel, piece.

H6596.strongs:
Origin: or פֹּתָה; (Ezekiel 13:19), from an unused root meaning to open;
Meaning: a hole, i.e. hinge or the female pudenda
KJV renders: hinge, secret participle

H6597.strongs:
Origin: or פִּתְאֹם; from 6621;
Meaning: instantly
KJV renders: straightway, sudden(-ly).

H6598.strongs:
Origin: of Persian origin;
Meaning: a dainty
KJV renders: portion (provision) of meat.

H6599.strongs:
Origin: of Persian origin;
Meaning: a (judicial) sentence
KJV renders: decree, sentence.
